\name{ExchangeTradedFundConstituents}
\alias{ExchangeTradedFundConstituents}
\title{The instruments an exchange traded fund holds, with their weights}
\description{
An exchange traded fund is two things. The fund's units trade on the exchange at their own price, which \code{ExchangeTradedFund} reads, and the fund holds a basket of other instruments, which this class describes. \code{ExchangeTradedFund$constituents} returns the stored basket, and the basket's \code{fund} is the fund again.

Comparing the two says how well the fund does its job. \code{tracking_difference()} is the fund's return minus its holdings' return over a range, which is mostly its fees, and the inherited \code{tracking_error(benchmark = basket$fund)} is how unevenly it follows them. \code{premium_or_discount} compares the fund's price now with its indicative net asset value, which the exchange publishes as an index row such as \code{NIFTYBEES-NAV} when one is stored with the basket.

The generator carries \code{ExchangeTradedFundConstituents$KIND}, \code{"exchange_traded_fund_constituents"}.
}
\examples{
\dontrun{
fund <- ExchangeTradedFund$new(exchange = "nse", symbol = "NIFTYBEES")
holdings <- fund$constituents
gap <- holdings$tracking_difference(days = 365)
premium <- holdings$premium_or_discount

weights <- c(
  HDFCBANK = 13,
  ICICIBANK = 9,
  RELIANCE = 8.5,
  INFY = 5,
  BHARTIARTL = 4.5
)
members <- list()
for (symbol in names(weights)) {
  share <- Equity$new(exchange = "nse", symbol = symbol)
  members[[length(members) + 1]] <- BasketMember$new(
    share,
    weight = weights[[symbol]]
  )
}
holdings <- ExchangeTradedFundConstituents$new(
  name = "NIFTYBEES",
  members = members,
  fund = fund
)

cat(holdings$fund$symbol, holdings$fund$last_price, "\n")
unlinked <- ExchangeTradedFundConstituents$new(
  name = "unlinked",
  members = members
)
print(unlinked$fund)

print(holdings$premium_or_discount)
premium <- holdings$premium_or_discount
if (is.null(premium)) {
  symbol <- holdings$fund$symbol
  cat(sprintf("No indicative value is known for \%s.\n", symbol))
} else {
  cat(sprintf(
    "\%s trades at \%+.2f\%\% to its value\n",
    holdings$fund$symbol,
    premium
  ))
}
}

